#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:2
msgctxt "s-9d4e7261d377-0000"
msgid "Register machines and counter machines"
msgstr "Máquinas de registros y máquinas de contadores"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:6
msgctxt "s-94cf2354335c-0001"
msgid ""
"A register machine stores its values in a few numbered boxes called "
"registers. Real processors are register machines. The smallest version, a "
"*counter machine*, has only two operations: add one to a register, or "
"subtract one and jump if the result is zero. It exists as a thinking tool: "
"it is simple enough to prove things about, yet powerful enough to compute "
"anything (two counters are enough). Several entries are register machines in"
" disguise. CMake's ⟦CODE_0001⟧ to ⟦CODE_0002⟧ are the registers of "
"⟦MACRO_0003⟧. .NET's balancing groups, in ⟦MACRO_0004⟧, are a counter."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina de registros guarda sus valores en unas pocas casillas numeradas"
" que se llaman registros. Los procesadores reales son máquinas de registros."
" La versión más pequeña, una *máquina de contadores*, solo tiene dos "
"operaciones: sumar uno a un registro o restarle uno y saltar si el resultado"
" es cero. Sirve para razonar. Es lo bastante simple como para demostrar sus "
"propiedades y lo bastante potente como para calcular cualquier cosa (bastan "
"dos contadores). Varias entradas son máquinas de registros disfrazadas. En "
"CMake, de ⟦CODE_0001⟧ a ⟦CODE_0002⟧ son los registros de ⟦MACRO_0003⟧. Los "
"grupos de equilibrio de .NET en ⟦MACRO_0004⟧ forman un contador."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:10
msgctxt "s-05c2d79033db-0002"
msgid ""
"A register machine names its storage cells; a counter machine needs only "
"increment, decrement and a zero test"
msgstr ""
"Una máquina de registros identifica sus celdas. Una máquina de contadores "
"solo necesita sumar, restar y comprobar si llega a cero"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:11
msgctxt "s-dc2a5741e8a5-0003"
msgid ""
"Two panels. In the register machine, registers R1 and R2 hold 19 and 23. The"
" instruction ADD R1, R2 into R1 leaves R1 holding 42 and R2 still holding "
"23. In the counter machine, counters C1 and C2 start at 2 and 0. A loop "
"decrements C1, increments C2 and tests C1 for zero. If C1 is not zero, the "
"loop runs again. When C1 reaches zero, C1 is 0 and C2 is 2."
msgstr ""
"Dos paneles. En la máquina de registros, los registros R1 y R2 contienen 19 "
"y 23. La instrucción ADD R1, R2 guarda el resultado en R1. R1 queda con 42 y"
" R2 conserva 23. En la máquina de contadores, C1 y C2 empiezan en 2 y 0. Un "
"bucle decrementa C1, incrementa C2 y comprueba si C1 vale cero. Si C1 no "
"vale cero, el bucle se ejecuta de nuevo. Cuando C1 llega a cero, C1 vale 0 y"
" C2 vale 2."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:12
msgctxt "s-8806c4f1ffde-0004"
msgid "Counter machine"
msgstr "Máquina de contadores"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:14
msgctxt "s-4d9292ebb84f-0005"
msgid "C1 = 2, C2 = 0"
msgstr "C1 = 2, C2 = 0"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:14
msgctxt "s-599daa3dc4c7-0006"
msgid "DEC C1, INC C2"
msgstr "DEC C1, INC C2"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:15
msgctxt "s-afeca60fe8d5-0007"
msgid "C1 is zero?"
msgstr "¿C1 vale cero?"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:16
msgctxt "s-755a4564a52b-0008"
msgid "no: loop"
msgstr "no: repite el bucle"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:17
msgctxt "s-8a798890fe93-0009"
msgid "yes"
msgstr "sí"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:17
msgctxt "s-56f55f30524f-0010"
msgid "C1 = 0, C2 = 2"
msgstr "C1 = 0, C2 = 2"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:19
msgctxt "s-e625e43cae65-0011"
msgid "Register machine"
msgstr "Máquina de registros"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:21
msgctxt "s-f7a6300c1952-0012"
msgid "R1 = 19, R2 = 23"
msgstr "R1 = 19, R2 = 23"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:21
msgctxt "s-bbf6b7537363-0013"
msgid "ADD R1, R2 into R1"
msgstr "ADD R1, R2 a R1"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:21
msgctxt "s-1000358d589c-0014"
msgid "R1 = 42, R2 = 23"
msgstr "R1 = 42, R2 = 23"

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:25
msgctxt "s-ba821a1159c4-0015"
msgid ""
"On the left, the instruction names its cells (⟦CODE_0001⟧ and ⟦CODE_0002⟧). "
"On the right, the machine has two counters and three moves: count down, "
"count up and test for zero. Moving a count from ⟦CODE_0003⟧ to ⟦CODE_0004⟧ "
"takes one pass of the loop for each unit, so a counter machine is slow on "
"purpose. What it shows is how little machinery is enough."
msgstr ""
"A la izquierda, la instrucción nombra sus celdas (⟦CODE_0001⟧ y "
"⟦CODE_0002⟧). A la derecha, la máquina tiene dos contadores y tres acciones:"
" contar hacia abajo, contar hacia arriba y comprobar si el valor es cero. "
"Pasar la cuenta de ⟦CODE_0003⟧ a ⟦CODE_0004⟧ requiere una vuelta del bucle "
"por unidad. Por eso una máquina de contadores es lenta a propósito. Muestra "
"con qué poca maquinaria basta."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:27
msgctxt "s-ab8479dda763-0016"
msgid ""
"**Use it when:** you want to explain what a strange system *is*, by finding "
"its registers."
msgstr ""
"**Úsala cuando:** quieras explicar qué *es* un sistema insólito al "
"identificar sus registros."

#: lessons/cs-source/concepts/register-machine.md:28
msgctxt "s-5e6b5191d81e-0017"
msgid ""
"**Avoid it as a coding style:** it is a model for reasoning, not a way to "
"write programs."
msgstr ""
"**Evítala como estilo de programación:** es un modelo para razonar, no una "
"forma de escribir programas."

